<Placemark><name>ccg/2026/NW-P-1503</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-10-30T02:45:00Z to 2026-11-03T08:30:00Z

Marine Works - Diving Operations - Vancouver Harbour
Diving Operations East of Second Narrows, on the South side of the channel near the FRPD McKenzie derrick in the vicinity of 49 17.650N 123 01.155W.
Hours of Operation;
Day 1, 30 Oct 2026 2330 UTC to 31 Oct 2026 0330 UTC,
Day 2, 31 Oct 2026 2345 UTC to 01 Nov 2026 0500 UTC,
Day 3, 02 Nov 2026 0130 UTC to 02 Nov 2026 0630 UTC,
Day 4, 03 Nov 2026 0300 UTC to 03 Nov 2026 0830 UTC.
Mariner requested to detour North a minimum of 100 meters.
During active diving operations, the following vessel traffic measures will apply:
 - 100 metres separation is required from the dive operation.
 - Light tugs and commercial vessels may be permitted to transit on the north side of the channel at a slow but safe speed, provided the required separation can be maintained.
   - Should your tier 2 vessel require a lift of the Second Narrows Rail Bridge, it should be entered into the Centralized Scheduling System.
- Tier 1 vessels and tug &amp; barges will be unable to transit during the times posted above. Please plan your transits around these scheduled times.
Vessels monitoring VHF Channels 12, 16 and 69.
Minimum wash
                                                    Cancels NW-P-1502-26</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>-123.0192,49.2942,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>ccg/2026/NW-M-1570</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-10-30T02:01:00Z to until cancelled

Scientific Instruments Change - LaHave Bank
Wave Glider C34167NS is transiting from 42 21.000N 065 12.500W along the following coordinates in sequence:
42 28.000N 065 00.630W
 42 48.180N 064 17.022W
 43 03.360N 063 47.280W
 43 18.960N 063 31.075W
Wave glider c34164NS is copper in colour with a mast extending 1.2 metres above the surface of the water, supporting a solid white light and orange visibility flag and is equipped with a non-transmitting AIS receiver.
It is remotely operated, moving at a speed of approximately 1.0 knots and measuring 3.05 metres by 0.81 metres.
For further information, authorities and mariners may contact Sue L’Orsa at 250-877-8052, Tyler Byrne 902-719-7078, or Liquid Robotics Wave Glider Operations Centre at +1 888-574-4574 or 408-636-4205
                                                    Cancels NW-M-1525-26</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>-65.2083,42.35,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-65.0105,42.4667,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-64.2837,42.803,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-63.788,43.056,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-63.5179,43.316,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
