<Placemark><name>ccg/2026/NW-M-1553</name><styleUrl>#a</styleUrl><description>2026-10-26T15:17:00Z to until cancelled

Scientific Instruments Change - East Scotian Slope
Wave Glider C34167NS is transiting from 43 34.410 N 060 13.232 W along the following coordinates in sequence:
43 23.107 N 061 02.750 W,
43 03.695 N 062 05.043 W,
42 47.730 N 063 13.013 W.
Wave glider C34164NS is copper in colour with a mast extending 1.2 metres above the surface of the water, supporting a solid white light and orange visibility flag and is equipped with a non-transmitting ais receiver. It is remotely operated, moving at a speed of approximately 1.2 knots and measuring 3.05 metres by 0.81 metres.
For further information, authorities and mariners may contact sue l’orsa at 250-877-8052, tyler byrne at 902-719-7078, or liquid robotics wave glider operations centre at +1 888-574-4574 or 408-636-420
                                                    Cancels NW-M-1522-26</description><MultiGeometry><Point><coordinates>-60.2205,43.5735,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-61.0458,43.3851,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-62.084,43.0616,0</coordinates></Point><Point><coordinates>-63.2169,42.7955,0</coordinates></Point></MultiGeometry></Placemark>
